.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/SEAL-PACKAGE-DRAFT-2026-09-08.md:24:The declared four-process evaluator uses deterministic round-robin sharding and catalogue-order reduction. Serial/parallel results and receipt counts are exact-equality tested. The predeclared fallback sequence ended at one boundary per forecast offset and M=48.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/SEAL-PACKAGE-DRAFT-2026-09-08.md:26:On three real quarantined a-r0 decisions, catalogue counts were 997, 997 and 966. Decision times were 9.920572, 8.879807 and 5.949833 s: mean 8.250071 s, p95 9.816495 s, maximum 9.920572 s. Complete-anchor totals were 21.315449, 20.119099 and 20.540675 s: mean 20.658408 s, p95 21.237972 s. Thus both the <10 s selection and <60 s per-anchor gates pass. Provider construction was 20.222051 s once/world.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/SEAL-PACKAGE-DRAFT-2026-09-08.md:69:The independent validity ledger is `LINK-CLOSURE-LEDGER-2026-09-09.md`; it closes 19.196747 dB C/N at boresight and 9.851770 dB at the half-power edge and reproduces 618.475972 Mbit/s beam capacity with n=13 as the first 50-Mbit/s occupancy infeasible at any SINR.
