src/mcrl/algorithms/ee_axis_lcsrs_three_route.py:7:This module owns no teacher, simulator, coalition selector, or retry.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-4C-AUDIT-ROWS-2026-09-08.md:6:3. **Row 12/26 (deadline before validation):** per the 4c-gate decision the 2^|A| validation no longer exists; the runner timer covers catalogue → selection → validation and executes the validated BASE on a miss for every set arm, including large coalitions (no exception path).
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **Executable set-score decomposition (from the review's pass 1(d)).** For a configuration with changed-user set A relative to the anchor reference a⁰ and F = B − η_ref·E: unilateral increments dᵢ = F(aᵢ, a⁰₋ᵢ) − F(a⁰); interaction residual Ψ_A = F(a_A, a⁰₋A) − F(a⁰) − Σᵢ∈A dᵢ. C1(config) = Σᵢ∈A dᵢ (+ Φ), C3(config) = Ψ_A (credited to users by the Shapley allocation of the interaction game; pairs = Ψ/2 each), C2(config) = the declared continuation value excluding the immediate term. Identity: C1 + C3 = F(a_A) − F(a⁰) exactly (KAT). Factor arms: FULL = C1 + C2 + C3; DROP_C1 = C2 + C3; DROP_C2 = C1 + C3; DROP_C3 = C1 + C2 (additive), all in the same selector class and catalogue (stage-4 item 18).
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:10:6. **Information contract for C3 (residual risk 0.90).** Before any successor training, the stages 6–8 contract v1 must state exactly what the learned heads observe and what the coordinator computes (candidate identities, load, shared capacity and interference, activation state, other users' proposed actions or a joint search), with the deployment-capability manifest; retrained ablations are the scientific claim, checkpoint knockouts are reported separately.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.3-ERRATUM-2026-09-08.md:6:v1.2 §1 says "Total: 28 primary-eligible cells + diagnostic U cells". The explicit list in the same paragraph governs and yields **25 primary-eligible settings** (5 architecture baselines `a-r0, a′-r0, a-γ0, b0, a′-γ0` + S, H, SH, T for each of the five = 5 + 4 × 5) plus **6 diagnostic U settings** (`U-cap`, `U-margin` for `a-γ, b, a′-γ`; v1.2 §2), i.e. **31 settings in total**. The number 28 was a counting error; the explicit enumeration, its sealed priority order and the matrix digests of engine stage 2 (31 settings) are the authority. Flagged by the stage-2 engine report before any setting was evaluated on a real world.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:3:Source: provider v1 report — with the Python-object tape, the 57 525-chain cross-product inventory and the unbatched runner, the measured cost is 12.63 s per anchor of provider acquisition, 4.66 s per 48-boundary catalogue row, q ≈ 0.308, ≈ 182 868 core-hours for the plan (budget: 160). This is an engineering failure of the current implementation, not a property of the physics; the decisions below fix the implementation first and only then thin the plan, in a pre-declared order.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:5:1. **Engineering targets (stage 4, before any thinning):** dense per-step numpy tapes (provider decision 9); realisable inventory only (≈ 2 760 chains, decision 4/D4); batched evaluation of a whole catalogue per anchor — the capped fixed point, ACM lookup, energy and bits computed for all configurations of an anchor in one vectorised pass over (configuration × boundary); provider acquisition amortised once per world (48 × 30 boundaries computed once and shared by all settings and arms). Target: ≤ 0.02 s per catalogue row per anchor and ≤ 1 s per anchor of provider work on the reference hardware; the rehearsal reports both.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:7:3. **Thinning order if the rehearsed projection still exceeds 160 core-hours** (apply the smallest step that fits; record every applied step in the seal; never chosen by outcome): (i) anchor stride k = 2, then 3 (decision item 3); (ii) treatment settings dropped from the **bottom of the sealed priority order** (T cells first, then SH, then H, then S — within each, the lowest-priority architectures first); the five architecture baselines `a-r0, a′-r0, a-γ0, b0, a′-γ0` and the U diagnostics are never dropped; (iii) probe worlds reduced from 4 to 3 only if (i)–(ii) are insufficient, and then the claim is labelled accordingly.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md:13:- **Everything else** follows astra round 3 §2 (items 1, 3, 5–31 unchanged: ACM table, margin, served ⇔ SINR ≥ −1.4418 dB after joint resolution, energy accounting with P_idle = 0 primary, clock/integration, geometry/10° visibility, actions, observable information, calibration λ = η_ref and κ on a nominal-greedy reference, reward core R = B − η_ref·E, Φ as QoS, C1 full-network difference surplus, C2 feature migration and forecast schema, C3 as set-level consolidation coordinator, learning contract, history seal) and §3 (known-answer suite, extended for (a) with coupled-power convergence/saturation and slot-consistent interference fixtures).
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGE2-2026-09-08.md:8:4. **Catalogue census** — **CHANGE** for real worlds: the complete Cartesian product of legal assignments is used only when it has ≤ 4 096 configurations (synthetic worlds). Otherwise the union catalogue is the bounded set: (i) every unilateral move of every user to every legal option; (ii) the S0 deployable proposals (top-two per user) and all frozen beam evacuations; (iii) all pairwise joint moves among the top-K = 10 users ranked by nominal unilateral surplus, over all their legal option pairs; (iv) per-active-beam evacuation sets (every user of the beam to its best legal alternative). J1 = the best changed-user-count > 1 configuration in this catalogue; U1 = the best in (i). The catalogue definition and its digest are sealed; the per-world superset check of stage-3 item 10 reports how many legal options fall outside the shortlist.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-PIPELINE-AUDITS-CD-2026-09-08.md:13:9. **C2 forecasts (D-N8; ENGINE):** forecasts use nominal geometry and nominal interference only (no realised fading), survival is the focal user's, an INVALID solve makes the forecast INVALID (no surrogate), the uncapped required-power margin is reported even when negative. KATs for each.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-PIPELINE-AUDITS-CD-2026-09-08.md:16:12. **Timing (D-N12; ENGINE):** the decision timer covers proposal generation, forecasts, catalogue evaluation, selection, validation and fallback; the cost estimate counts actual provider/power calls; cached lookups are not decision time.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-PROVIDER-2026-09-08.md:5:1. **T7 — intra-satellite co-colour interference (protocol CHANGE, engine stage 4 + provider):** `PrimitiveCandidate` cross gains are keyed by physical aggressor **(NORAD, beam-chain)**, not by NORAD alone, so that co-colour beams of the same satellite are representable; the interference sum in `architectures.py` consumes the per-chain map; the provider emits per-chain cross gains (aggressor boresight = its own served cell, co-colour only). KAT: a fixture with two co-colour beams on one satellite serving neighbouring cells reproduces the legacy same-satellite interference term.
