/home/sat/mcrl-v025-provenance-ws/CONSTANT-PROVENANCE-2026-09-09.md:265:At cap, `γi(Ni+Ii)/gi > ci` means the desired target cannot be reached at that joint operating point. A unique clipped solution is not proof of uncapped SINR feasibility, and still less a delivered-rate guarantee. A user can be exactly at cap and meet its target at equality; “cap hit” and “infeasible” are not logically identical. A missing rate-target mode forces cap regardless of that placeholder target.
