/home/sat/mcrl-v025-witness-ws/PSI-WITNESS-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:17:The engine calls `B−eta_ref·E` its physical objective and stores a separate negative, dimensionless handover preference `phi`. To match the question's positive cost notation, this report uses Phi_cost=−kappa·phi and **F=B−eta_ref·E−Phi_cost**. Same-satellite moves cost kappa/2 each; satellite changes cost kappa each. These costs are additive and cancel exactly from Psi. Both physical-core F and full F are saved in the evidence. The engine's `set_score_decomposition` computes Psi and checks the physical identity; the harness additionally checks `(factor_c1+C3)·kappa=Delta F` exactly, including the preference.
